     This Protection applies only at pair-level, and will never lock all pairs globally.
     This Protection does not consider `lookback_period` as it only looks at the latest trade.
 
+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at the trades for a pair that closed within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), ordered from most-recent to oldest, and counts an unbroken streak of losing trades (a trade with a profit below `required_profit`, default `0.0`) starting from the most recent trade.
+As soon as a win (or a trade with a profit at or above `required_profit`) is encountered, the streak stops counting. If the streak reaches `trade_limit` or more consecutive losses, the pair is locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) - preventing the bot from re-entering that pair while whatever is going wrong for it keeps going wrong.
+
+Unlike [`StoplossGuard`](#stoploss-guard) or [`LowProfitPairs`](#low-profit-pairs), this only reacts to *consecutive* losses in a row - a single winning trade resets the streak, and past losses that aren't part of the current unbroken streak are ignored.
+
+This applies across all pairs, unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which will then only look at one pair at a time - allowing a losing streak on one pair to be handled independently from a losing streak bot-wide.
+
+Similarly, this protection will by default look at all trades (long and short). For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of long losses.
+
+The below example stops trading for all pairs for 12 candles as soon as 4 consecutive losing trades occurred within the last 48 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 48,
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
